<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.48.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.48.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.48.0 (2026-11-25): The story of scope change SC11_NoAnalogies is done. Build commit a1a6ecf."""@en .

ex:TK11_NoAnalogies_Content backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "New content 4.3.0 (chapter 10) and 4.4.0 (chapter 11): twelve slides, the summary and practice sentences, two part cards and the title-slide phrase now state each concept plainly; the box label is IN SHORT and the table head What it is and does. Notes 4.4.0 rewritten for the twelve slides and the notes that named a comparison (all 60 to 140 words). The one phrase hit in the chapter 10 code source (a shelf works like a dictionary) and the word cursor are the technical terms of the book, not everyday comparisons, so the source stays 1.3.0 (chapter 11 source has no hit)." .
ex:TK11_NoAnalogies_Rebuild backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Builder 2.9.0 (label, table head and title phrase come from the spec; unchanged specs build as before), standard check 1.3.0 (D4 accepts the IN SHORT box beside the old markers), decks 4.5.0 and 4.4.0 (41 slides each), manifests 1.7.0, lecture exports for both chapters (the chapter 10 lecture had still described the earlier 24-slide deck), page data and pages 9.25.0 and 9.26.0. Previous versions stay." .
ex:TK11_NoAnalogies_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck checks (standard, fit, layout, notes, overlap, reader notes, story prose) pass for both decks after shortening table rows that had wrapped into the slide number on chapter 10; code check C1 to C5: 0 findings (18 and 19 examples); full page tests 9.41.0: 410 and 414 features passed, 0 failed; a word search of both decks, notes, lecture files, sources and pages finds no everyday comparison. Known limits: the code example name Where you stand (chapter 10, source 1.3.0) is a figure of speech for the working directory and was left because the name must match across source, manifest, deck and page; other chapters still carry their analogies (out of scope); the story repeat check still reports 2 pairs to read, both the shared name Ken Thompson (chapter 10 dbm story with a chapter 8 and a chapter 9 story); they are older than this change and not touched by it." .
ex:ST11_NoAnalogies backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met for chapters 10 and 11, with the known limits named in the verify task." .
